  "body": "**Fixes #722.** `verify` said `\"ok\": true` for a program whose post was then refused by the ops' own warnings. So `camcraft-cli process <project>` (no `-o`) exited 0, \"clean\", for a job it couldn't post.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **`crates/app/src/script/api.rs`, `v_verify`:** behind `cam.verify`, `cam.check` and the MCP `verify` tool, and through them the CLI's exit code.\n  - `ok` now also requires that no op in scope holds the post with its own cached warnings.\n  - The rule is the post's own, in the new `holds_post`: a suppressed op is not in the program, and a warning counts exactly when `Warning::blocks_post()` is true. That is when `posting::stream_records` writes it as a `WARN` record, and any `WARN` record refuses the post. A Scallop or ProbeSearch note still doesn't count.\n  - The report gains `held_by`: the labels of the ops in scope holding the post, empty when none.\n- **`assets/scripts/cam.d.ts` and its template in `crates/app/src/script/mod.rs`:** `VerifyReport` documents `ok` and the new `held_by` (the bindings drift test keeps the two equal).\n- **`crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`:** the `verify` tool's description says what `ok` and `held_by` mean.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/722-verify-ok-warnings.md`.\n\nWhat stays the same: the program gate (`posting::verification_report`), the post's refusal text, and the findings list. Only the summary now agrees with them.\n\n**Behaviour change, intended:** `camcraft-cli process <project>` without `-o` now exits 1 (\"the job is not clean\") for a job whose ops' warnings would refuse the post. Before, it exited 0.\n\n### Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/mcp_verify.rs`, new)\n\nThe fixture is a real collision. `EM-0400-2FL` is a Ø4 cutter with 12 mm of flute on a Ø6 shank, so contouring a 30 mm wall rubs the shank on the part below the flutes (84 `shank_hit` findings). A 10 mm wall stays inside the flutes and is clean.\n\n- `verify_is_not_ok_while_an_ops_own_warnings_hold_the_post`: the 30 mm job has a fresh op and a passing gate, and every finding blocks the post. `ok` is `false`, `held_by` is `[\"C1\"]` (the same answer for `verify {name: \"C1\"}`), and the post is still refused with \"warning(s)\".\n- `a_contour_inside_the_flutes_still_verifies_ok_and_posts`: the 10 mm neighbour has no findings, `ok: true`, `held_by: []`, and the post writes.\n- `the_cli_process_lane_exits_one_for_a_job_its_warnings_hold`: both jobs saved as projects and run through the real `camcraft-cli process`. The 30 mm job exits 1 with \"not clean\", the 10 mm job exits 0.\n\nWith `api.rs` put back to `main`, all three fail. The first fails at `a program the post refuses is not ok`, and the CLI test because the held job exits 0. The neighbour fails too, but only because `held_by` is a new key.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local)\n\nFork: `austin62jake/Camcraft2`, `main` at upstream f42d3788 (contains v0.16.0, PROCESS_VERSION 4). Gated on 43943371.\n\n- **Quick gate plan** (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`), plus the other suites that read verify's `ok` (`mcp_setup`, `mcp_live`, `mcp_render`, `contour_arc_sim`, `wall_column_gouge`, `program_entry`), run by hand at `-j 4`. No failures, nothing ignored.\n  - App lib: 103 passed.\n  - Suites: `cli` 7, `contour_arc_sim` 1, `mcp` 13, `mcp_live` 10, `mcp_pick` 2, `mcp_pockets` 3, `mcp_render` 5, `mcp_setup` 4, `mcp_verify` 3, `post_not_judged` 4, `program_entry` 9, `scripting` 18 (including the bindings drift test), `setup_mounts_post` 6, `wall_column_gouge` 3.\n- **Clippy:** `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`, clean.\n- **The original report**, reproduced by hand on `main` f42d3788 with `camcraft-cli mcp` and `camcraft-cli process` (see #722).\n- **Not run:** Linux, macOS, the batch tier. The GUI is untouched: its status line reads `verification_report`, which this PR doesn't change.\n\nChangelog: `verify` (and `camcraft-cli process` without `-o`) no longer reports a job as clean when an operation's own warnings would refuse the post; the report names those operations under `held_by` (#722)\n\nFixes #722\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
